ipur district and neighbouring parts of Madhya Pradesh, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ratibor-i-duke-of-pomerania"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ratibor-i-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ratibor I, Duke of Pomerania</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ratibor I was a Pomeranian duke of the Griffin dynasty who ruled after the murder of his brother Wartislaw I around 1135 until his death in 1156.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ratna-malla"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ratna-malla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ratna Malla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ratna Malla was the first king of Kantipur (Kathmandu), one of the three Malla kingdoms of the Kathmandu Valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ratnagiri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ratnagiri</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ratnagiri is a port town on the Konkan coast of Maharashtra, western India, and the headquarters of a district of the same name.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri-odisha"><span class="enc-name">Ratnagiri (Odisha)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ratnagiri is a Buddhist site in the Jajpur district of Odisha, India, part of the 'Diamond Triangle' with Lalitagiri and Udayagiri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ratnasimha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ratnasimha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ratnasimha</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rat